---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MailtoCta from '../../components/MailtoCta.astro';
import { email, links, pageTitle, subjects } from '../../data/site';

const description =
  'Vendor-neutral, privacy-minded smart environments, typically Home Assistant-centred, with local control where it matters.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageTitle('Smart environments')}
  description={description}
  currentPath="/services/smart-environment"
>
  <div class="page-wrap">
    <article class="prose-measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">Exploratory conversation. Not a fixed product package.</p>
      <h1>Smart environments</h1>

      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Homeowners and small properties that want automation without surrendering everything to a
        single consumer cloud.
      </p>

      <h2>Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Devices don’t talk; DIY setups get brittle; privacy and maintainability suffer when
        architecture is an afterthought.
      </p>

      <h2>Positive proposition</h2>
      <p>
        We design, build, and operate vendor-neutral, privacy-minded smart environments, typically
        Home Assistant-centred, with local control where it matters, documented cloud dependencies
        where they remain, and architecture you can operate. These are installations we build and
        operate. This site is not a client delivery portfolio.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="card-grid card-grid--features">
      <article class="card card--static">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>
            Local-first Home Assistant design and build on dedicated on-prem hardware
            (containerised, Postgres-backed). Cloud only where a device requires it.
          </li>
          <li>
            Vendor-neutral integration: Zigbee/ZHA, Somfy/Overkiz local API, Nest/Blink where kept,
            mixed Tuya/Aqara/SONOFF/Hue ecosystems. Open coordinators, not a single vendor hub.
          </li>
          <li>
            Custom integration engineering (ZHA quirks, ESPHome, upstream contributions).
          </li>
          <li>
            Presence and occupancy (mmWave / ESPHome) driving lighting, climate, and privacy
            automations.
          </li>
          <li>
            Voice and everyday control (minimal, deliberate Alexa exposure; Home Assistant Voice;
            household dashboards).
          </li>
          <li>Ongoing operations (runbooks, session logs, remote support).</li>
          <li>AI-assisted home operations as emerging and exploratory only.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="card card--static">
        <h2>NucBox (hardened on-prem host)</h2>
        <p>
          The on-prem home server (NucBox-class mini-PC) we use for installations we build and
          operate. We do not sell this hardware and we do not have an OEM partnership.
        </p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Encrypted disk with TPM unlock</li>
          <li>Tailscale-only administration</li>
          <li>No inbound ports</li>
          <li>Encrypted nightly backups mirrored off-site</li>
          <li>Containerised Home Assistant and Postgres</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="card__meta">
          <a href={links.starlinkStack}>Starlink monitoring stack</a>
          {' · '}
          <a href={links.zhaDeviceHandler}>ZHA device-handler PR</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="card card--static">
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Local-first control, with every kept cloud dependency documented.</li>
          <li>
            Privacy-respecting cameras: Frigate, presence-gated recording, and network controls so
            footage stays local.
          </li>
          <li>
            Home network resilience: DNS, reverse proxy and TLS on the LAN, mesh Wi-Fi, Tailscale
            remote access, ISP/Starlink monitoring, off-site backups.
          </li>
          <li>
            Hardened host bootstrap as on the NucBox card (encrypted disk, Tailscale-only admin, no
            inbound ports, encrypted off-site backups).
          </li>
          <li>Not a certified alarm, medical, or life-safety installer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="card__meta">
          <a href={links.internetPi}>internet-pi contribution</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="section prose-measure">
      <h2>Public engineering artefacts</h2>
      <ul class="list">
        <li>
          <a href={links.haForumFieldNotes}>Home Assistant community forum field notes</a> (SONOFF
          roller-shutter switch)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={links.zhaDeviceHandler}>ZHA device-handler contribution</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={links.starlinkStack}>Open-source Starlink monitoring stack</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={links.internetPi}>internet-pi contribution</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Hands-on Home Assistant, Zigbee, and ESPHome work since 2024.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose-measure">
      <h2>What a first conversation covers</h2>
      <ol class="numbered-tight">
        <li>Goals and constraints (privacy, local-first preference, household users, existing kit).</li>
        <li>
          Boundary map: what must stay local. Life-safety and alarm limits we will not overclaim.
        </li>
        <li>A non-binding architecture sketch and staged scope if a project were to proceed.</li>
        <li>
          An honest fit check, including when DIY or another specialist is the better next step.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Example outputs (only if we continue under a separate agreement)</h2>
      <p>
        Architecture notes; integration plan; configured system in agreed scope; automation
        packages; owner runbook.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Deeper project documentation will come later.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p class="callout__label">Boundaries</p>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>Vendor-neutral: we do not exist to push a single OEM.</li>
          <li>Not a claim of certified alarm, medical, or life-safety installer status.</li>
          <li>
            We do not publish a portfolio of completed <em>client</em> Home Assistant deployments on
            this site.
          </li>
          <li>We do not claim Matter, Thread, Z-Wave, or LoRaWAN support.</li>
          <li>
            Trip and Move demonstrate product engineering. They do not prove smart-environment
            consulting delivery.
          </li>
          <li>No pricing or fixed outcomes from a first email.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Start a conversation</h2>
      <p>
        Email <strong>{email}</strong> with property type, what you already run, privacy priorities,
        and the one problem you most want solved.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Subject suggestion: <span class="mono">{subjects.smartEnvironment}</span></p>
      <MailtoCta subject={subjects.smartEnvironment} label={`Email ${email}`} />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
